From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] CurlFile: a request cancelled on purpose is not an error

CCurlFile::Cancel() lets another thread end a transfer: it sets the
read state's m_cancelled, FillBuffer() then returns no data, and
Open() sees no HTTP response. Open() logged that at LOGERROR as
"Failed with code 0", the same as a server that cannot be reached, so
every request its caller chose to end - a subtitle translation dropped
by a seek, say - left an error in the log.

When m_cancelled is set, the same line is now logged at LOGDEBUG. A
failure with no cancellation is logged as before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp b/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
index be9e0c2..41421c7 100644
--- a/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
@@ -1179,8 +1179,9 @@ bool CCurlFile::Open(const CURL& url)
       ReadLine(error.data(), 4095);
     }
 
-    CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "CCurlFile::{} - <{}> Failed with code {}:\n{}", __FUNCTION__,
-              redactPath, m_httpresponse, error);
+    CLog::Log(m_state->m_cancelled ? LOGDEBUG : LOGERROR,
+              "CCurlFile::{} - <{}> Failed with code {}:\n{}", __FUNCTION__, redactPath,
+              m_httpresponse, error);
 
     return false;
   }
